/-!
# Checked descent data for the native octad graph

The octad stabilizer carries every vertex to one of four representatives.
The certificate supplies words in its actual generators, the thirty neighbors
of each representative, a lower common neighbor for every horizontal edge,
and a spanning tree on its lower neighbors. Each tree edge is filled by a
square whose remaining vertex has lower rank.

The rank is determined by intersection size with the marked octad: 8, 0, 4,
and 2 correspond to ranks 0, 1, 2, and 3. The proof only needs the explicit
rank function, not a separate distance-transitivity theorem. All evaluations
are checked by the kernel. Orbit coverage is divided into blocks of at most
96 octads; neighbor coverage is checked one representative at a time. This
keeps reduction caches bounded. Declaration elaboration is sequential here
after a measured simultaneous check used about 14 GB.

The untrusted certificate search is in `FourGeneration/source/generate.py`.
Source: Aschbacher, *Sporadic Groups* (1994), Exercise 13.2(2), printed p.210,
and the rank-lowering geometry of 38.6–38.7, pp.207–208.
-/

